# Gora sanction (domain)

Authority: Bible §10.1–10.10, Law 8. Audit V4 is the failure this rule exists to stop.

## Non-negotiables

- A Beef Gora **exists only after** the Pope verb **SANCTION BEEF GORA**. Until then it is a petition or a recommendation — not a Gora.
- Combat is an **unmodified WoW duel** in the world. No addon combat, no rated matchmaking, no ELO/MMR/hidden rating, no combat analytics, no betting/wagering.
- **Ban the demo Gora (Audit V4):** no typed self-report result, no member-typed win/loss/draw, no `GrantGora` / points faucet, no pair-pay cooldown as product, no “Gora” that is two people typing an outcome.
- Software **proposes**; the Pope **ratifies**. Nothing auto-declares, auto-announces in the Pope’s voice, or generates flavor. Cards and HUD are mute. The software never narrates (§4.2, §4.4).
- Congregation clients are input + display. Witnesses report; they do not rule. No peer self-reported authority over outcomes (Law 5).

## Required loop (§10.1)

**Petition → assisted matchmaking → SANCTION BEEF GORA → mute fighter cards → congregation favor → unmodified duel → Pope ratifies → records → possible elevation.**

Do not skip sanction. Do not collapse this into challenge-and-type-a-result.

## Petition hygiene (§10.2)

- Petitions expire (freshness window; Bible default is **~the current event** — do not invent a TTL number).
- Pool shows only petitioners who are **present and alive**.
- Pope **one-tap dismisses**, consequence-free.
- Dismissed petitioner gets a **soft re-petition cooldown** (duration unspecified — do not invent one).
- A petition may **name a desired opponent**. The callout is official **only when the Pope announces it**, never when the software does.

## Ruleset is the Pope (§10.3)

- No standing rulebook, rules engine, picker, or stipulations database.
- Optional **one-line stipulation** at sanction, recorded on the card if the Pope attaches it. Software remembers the decree; it does not offer a menu of rules.
- Practice defaults (not a picker): come as you are; fight to the duel’s natural end; flee system message proposes **COWARDICE RECORDED**; interference/weirdness proposes **VOID**; disconnect — console suggests Void, rematch encouraged; rematches at the Pope’s pleasure.
- Level gap **~2** is historical **guidance** the matchmaker may show; the Pope may waive it.

## Matchmaking (§10.5)

Recommend only: level proximity, freshness, head-to-head, named-challenge requests, class displayed plainly. **No odds copy. No ratings. No pairing score. No ranked suggestion list as authority. No auto-sanction of the next pair.** Level gap ~2 is guidance, not a hard filter. The Pope decides. Software never SANCTION BEEF GORA.

## Sanction, mute cards, favor (§10.6)

- **SANCTION BEEF GORA** is one Director Console action. After sanction, the Church recognizes the result.
- **Mute cards** (tale of the tape): name, class/portrait, level, Church title, Gora record, defenses, relevant accolades, head-to-head line when they have history. Show; the Pope tells. No generated flavor, no auto-introductions.
- **Favor** is pick-a-side only. Render a split bar. Always visible to the Pope; congregation display is a **per-event Pope toggle** (default on). No favor scores, streaks, accuracy records, economy, or wagering.

## Fight HUD (§10.7) — Event Mode only

- Only in **Event Mode**, only during a **sanctioned** fight. Quiet Mode: no HUD, no favor surface, no Gora feed.
- Compact: both fighters — name, class color, level, title, record, defense count — head-to-head line, favor split beneath. Top-center default, movable. Appears at sanction; persists through the verdict beat; exits with the consequence.
- Live health is Appendix A item 1. **Defined fallback:** render everything except live health. Do **not** invent a health hack, nameplate scrape, or combat-log HP estimator.

## Adjudication verbs (§10.8)

Duel system messages **propose**. The Pope ratifies with one action:

| Verb | Use |
|------|-----|
| **DECLARE VICTOR** | Pope names the winner |
| **COWARDICE RECORDED** | First-class flee outcome |
| **VOID** | Interference / weirdness; one tap, no shame |
| **Free ruling** | Any other Pope judgment (do not invent extra typed outcomes) |

The record stores the **Pope’s ruling**, not the parser’s guess. Elevation, when earned, is its own beat — never auto.

## Elevation — Lord milestone (§10.4)

A **Beef Knight** who **wins a sanctioned Gora the Pope judges fair** has earned elevation. “Fair” is entirely the Pope’s judgment. Attainable milestone; elevation is a Pope ceremony.

**Banned gates:** demotion, decay, mandatory defense, **beating a sitting Lord** (`goraLordWin` / sit-the-champ). **Defenses** is a Bible-named story field on the card and Records Book — not a title-defense schema, not a sit-the-champ gate, not a pairing score. Do not invent the increment rule (OPEN_QUESTIONS).

## Records are stories (§10.9–10.10)

- Character-level stories: wins/losses, **sanctioned-Gora W/L streaks only**, defenses, head-to-heads, notable victims, rulings received. Player profile aggregates; the **character** owns the Gora record (Law 7). Engagement, login, attendance, favor, and accuracy streaks remain banned.
- No damage meters, duration stats, per-class win rates, or other analytics.
- **Records Book** = parchment **superlatives**, never a ranked / sortable ladder. Bible MVP names: Most Sanctioned Victories, Longest Streak, Most Successful Defenses, The Iron Chin, Greatest Rivalry, **Famous Upsets (Pope-flagged — never computed)**, The Undefeated, The Glorious Martyr, Tournament Champions. Do not add a “#1 rating.”
- Permanence: no seasons, resets, decay, or expiry of old Gora records.

## Required Pope verbs (Gora)

`SANCTION BEEF GORA` · `DECLARE VICTOR` · `COWARDICE RECORDED` · `VOID` · free ruling · elevation when the Pope judges it earned.

## Do not rebuild

```text
❌ Challenge + typed RecordResult + Scoring:GrantGora
❌ Member/officer self-report as the Gora
❌ ELO / MMR / hidden rating / “fairness” score
❌ Favor as a scored game
❌ Auto-declare from duel chat
❌ Invented outcome enums beyond the verbs above
❌ HUD health workarounds
❌ Invented petition TTL / cooldown numbers
❌ Pairing score / auto-sanction / ranked matchmaking list
❌ Computed Famous Upsets
❌ Title-defense / sit-the-champ record schema
```
